  "id": "COMPOUND:43202 - PROTEIN:6304",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but interconnected relationship between 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One and Microtubule-associated protein 1B, with multiple pathways converging on the target protein. The drug appears to act through a series of intermediate targets, including Ataxin-2 and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn target Microtubule-associated protein 1B. These intermediates are all part of a broader family of compounds that modulate tubulin-related processes, suggesting a potential role in microtubule dynamics or stability. The evidence is consistent across different paths, with similar targets and downstream effects, indicating a possible mechanism involving the regulation of microtubule-associated proteins. The integration of these pathways highlights the drug's potential to influence microtubule function through a network of targets, emphasizing the importance of these proteins in cellular processes.",
